            <ArticleTitle>Meningeal neurosarcoidosis mimicking convexity en-plaque meningioma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>387-90</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 34-year old man presented with headaches. Computed tomography scanning revealed an enhancing subdural mass extending from the skull base to the convexity, thought to represent an en-plaque meningioma. Pathologic study revealed extraaxial subdural granulomatous inflammation consistent with neurosarcoidosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
